return {
["06:00"]={"Lying awake in my attic room, I hear a clock strike \003six\004 downstairs. It was fairly light and people were beginning to walk up and down the stairs.","Hunger","Knut Hamsun"},
["06:01"]={"In the image, he was looking straight up at the camera, holding a disposable cup in his hand. The time signature on the bottom right corner of the screen said that it was \00306:01\004 on the same morning the two of them had come to the convent.","The Passage","Justin Cronin"},
["06:02"]={"Bimingham New Street 5:25. Walsall 5:55. This train does not stop at Birchills, for reasons George has never been able to ascertain. Then it is Bloxwich \0036:02\004, Wyrley & Churchbridge 6:09. At 6:10 he nods to Mr. Merriman the stationmaster.","Arthur and George","Julian Barnes"},
["06:03"]={"It was still quite dark outside, and only the lower edge of the window-frame was white with snow. She could hear a low, mellow chime of bells; it was not the parish church, but somewhere further away. The watch on the little table showed \003three minutes past six\004.","The Party and Other Stories","Anton Pavlovich Chekhov"},
["06:04"]={"It was \003four minutes past six in the morning\004. She shivered. She waited. She stretched because she had sat in her car for three and a half hours before the milk float had turned into the street.","Heart of Danger","Gerald Seymour"},
["06:05"]={"A second man went in and found the shop empty, as he thought, at \003five minutes past six\004. That puts the time at between 5:30 and 6:05.","The ABC Murders","Agatha Christie"},
["06:07"]={"Hinton comes through the gate \003seven minutes after six\004. There must’ve been some traffic on the highway, or a delay during the security briefing. This morning his hair looks freshly cut, bringing out his high cheekbones and bright, hungry eyes.","The Dream Hotel","Laila Lalami"},
["06:08"]={"At \003six oh-eight a.m.\004 two men wearing ragged trench coats approached the Casino. The shorter of the men burst into flames.","Magic Bleeds","Ilona Andrews"},
["06:09"]={"\00306:09 CET\004\n“Why didn’t you wake me at four?” demanded Monti. He glared down at William, who was the same color as his soaking sheet, and was still sweating.","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer"},
["06:10"]={"The Chairman got out of bed at 7:20 and lit his first cigarette. He couldn’t remember exactly when he had woken. At \0036:10\004 he had phoned Tony, who was already up and waiting for his call.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["06:11"]={"“La Guardia,” said Dexter and then thanked the agent for sitting up half the night. Scott looked between the two front seats as the digital clock changed from \0036:11\004 to 6:12.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["06:12"]={"Doc Kerrison? The interrogation was surely unnecessary. Who else in this half-empty, echoing house would be answering at \0036:12 in the morning\004? He made no reply and the voice went on.","Death of an Expert Witness","P.D. James"},
["06:13"]={"It’s \00306:13\004. Ma says I ought to be wrapped up in Rug already, Old Nick might possibly come.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["06:14"]={"Virtual curtains mirrored her movement, sliding across the screen and dimming the room lighting. The red numbers \00306:14\004 faded but showed in the top right hand corner.","Mother Moon","Bob Goddard"},
["06:15"]={"Father expected his shaving-water to be ready at a \003quarter past six\004. Just seven minutes late, Dorothy took the can upstairs and knocked at her father’s door.","A Clergyman’s Daughter","George Orwell"},
["06:16"]={"And, as they boarded the \00306:16\004 to Mittelsteine, Erika toyed with the notion that although every metre of this journey took her further from her mother it would also bring her closer to the possibility of seeing Max again and the blossoming of their new little family.","Fifteen Words","Monika Jephcott Thomas"},
["06:17"]={"Dizzy, come on. He turned slowly, coaxing the animal down on to the pillow. The clock read \003six-seventeen\004. A second cat, Miles, purred on contentedly from the patch in the covers where Resnick’s legs had made a deep V.","Lonely Hearts","John Harvey"},
["06:18"]={"During the first fifteen minutes the “Argus” had the advantage of position, and at \003eighteen minutes after six\004 raked the “Pelican” at close range, but inflicted no great injury on the enemy’s hull or rigging, and killed at the utmost but one man, wounding only five.","History of the United States of America (Volume 7)","Henry Adams"},
["06:19"]={"\0036:19 am\004, 8th June 2004, the jet of your pupil set in the gold of your eye.","Venus","Carol Ann Duffy"},
["06:20"]={"It was \0036:20 a.m.\004, and my parents and I were standing, stunned and half-awake, in the parking lot of a Howard Johnson’s in Iowa.","Soon I Will Be Invincible","Austin Grossman"},
["06:22"]={"Clock overturned when he fell forward. That’ll give us the time of the crime. \003Twenty-two minutes past six\004.","The Murder at the Vicarage","Agatha Christie"},
["06:23"]={"It was \003twenty-three minutes past six\004. He actually thought about driving round and round Islington, with the radio on, shouting at it.","It Had to Be You","David Nobbs"},
["06:24"]={"Eventually I track the phone down by the green light on top. Notice that the time display reads \00306:24\004 before I answer. It’s Mum.","Simply Heaven","Serena Mackesy"},
["06:25"]={"Simon is happy to travel scum class when he’s on his own and even sometimes deliberately aims for the \0036:25\004. But today the .25 is delayed to 6:44.","The Deaths","Mark Lawson"},
["06:26"]={"No lights were on in the master bedroom at this time but it is noted that the official time of sunrise for this date is \0030626 hours\004. Victim is quite clear that sufficient light was entering via the large picture window to allow good visibility.","Roulette","Don and Linda Pendleton"},
["06:27"]={"\0036:27 A.M.\004\nEventually Mark could stand it no longer and at 6:30 A.M. he rose, showered, and put on a clean shirt and a fresh suit.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["06:28"]={"Thursday \0036:28 A.M.\004\nThe morning air was sharp and she wished she’d grabbed one of Adriana’s black knit shawls before going out. Could she pass for one of those stooped Greek peasant women? she wondered. Not likely. She shivered and pulled her thin coat around her.","Project Daedalus","Thomas Hoover"},
["06:29"]={"I sat up. There was a rug over me. I threw that off and got my feet on the floor. I scowled at a clock. The clock said \003a minute short of six-thirty\004.","The Big Sleep","Raymond Chandler"},
["06:30"]={"Tony gets up at \003six-thirty\004, as she always does. West sleeps on, groaning a little. Probably in his dreams he’s shouting; sounds in dreams are always louder.","The Robber Bride","Margaret Atwood"},
["06:31"]={"\0036:31 A.M.\004\n“Alpha Leader, this is SEAL One. I think we’ve spotted some hostiles.”","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["06:32"]={"BURBANK AIRPORT\n\0036:32 A.M.\004\nRush hour traffic crept forward in the pale morning light. Casey twisted her rearview mirror, and leaned over to check her makeup.","Airframe","Michael Crichton"},
["06:33"]={"Woke \0036:33 a.m.\004 Last session with Anderson. He made it plain he’s seen enough of me, and from now on I’m better alone. To sleep 8:00? (These count-downs terrify me.) He paused, then added: Goodbye, Eniwetok.","The Voices of Time","J.G. Ballard"},
["06:34"]={"\0036:34 A.M.\004\nThe leader of the SEALs, Lieutenant Devon Robbins, spoke into his thin microphone. “Can you see them? We could use an IR scope.” The SEALs had split into two teams, as was their practice, and he was leading the first.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["06:35"]={"My watch lay on the dressing-table close by; glancing at it, I saw that the time was \003twenty-five minutes to seven\004. I had been told that the family breakfasted at nine, so I had nearly two-and-a-half hours of leisure. Of course, I would go out, and enjoy the freshness of the morning.","Ravensdene Court","J.S. Fletcher"},
["06:36"]={"Kaldren pursues me like luminescent shadow. He has chalked up on the gateway ‘96,688,365,498,702’. Should confuse the mail man. Woke 9:05. To sleep \0036:36\004.","The Voices of Time","J.G. Ballard"},
["06:37"]={"\00306:37 GMT\004\nJackie didn’t need a wake-up call that morning. She was already on her way to Waterloo station by the time William was speeding down the M4.","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer"},
["06:38"]={"The clock on the dashboard said it was \0036:38 am\004. He left the keys in the car, and walked toward the tree.","American Gods","Neil Gaiman"},
["06:39"]={"He fired another torpedo at \0030639\004 hours from a distance of 500 metres. Again it missed its intended target, but exploded seven minutes later. The torpedos would only detonate on contact with a solid object.","Goldfinder","Keith Jessop and Neil Hanson"},
["06:40"]={"At eleven o’clock the phone rang, and still the figure did not respond, any more than it has responded when the phone had rung at twenty-five to seven in the morning, and again at \003twenty to seven\004","The Long Dark Tea-Time of the Soul","Douglas Adams"},
["06:41"]={"A car drove past at a crawl, its driver eyeing her curiously through the slow-moving windscreen wipers, and she pretended to rummage for something in her pocket, trying to look like a normal person, on her way to a normal day. It was \003nineteen minutes to seven\004.","The Horse Dancer","Jojo Moyes"},
["06:42"]={"It was \00306:42\004 and he had just finished his solo morning workout: three circuits of Ring 7 — the second-longest ring in the hab-disk — followed by a half hour pushing and pulling against resistance channels in the gym.","Marine Cadet","Tim C. Taylor"},
["06:43"]={"To London on the \0036:43 am\004. Jessica is back from her holiday. Things are looking up, she called me Chris, instead of Minister, when we talked on the phone this afternoon.","A View From the Foothills","Chris Mullin"},
["06:44"]={"Simon is happy to travel scum class when he’s on his own and even sometimes deliberately aims for the 6:25. But today the .25 is delayed to \0036:44\004.","The Deaths","Mark Lawson"},
["06:45"]={"He was still hurriedly thinking all this through, unable to decide to get out of the bed, when the clock struck \003quarter to seven\004. There was a cautious knock at the door near his head. “Gregor”, somebody called — it was his mother — “it’s quarter to seven. Didn’t you want to go somewhere?”","Metamorphosis","Franz Kafka"},
["06:46"]={"He bundled the papers on his desk into his briefcase and ran for the elevator. First piece of luck, it was on the top floor. Downstairs: \0036:46\004.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["06:48"]={"Car starts first time. Reliable Mercedes. Moves on the road: \0036:48\004. Must stay below speed limit. Never embarrass the Bureau.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["06:49"]={"Night ends, \0036:49\004. Meet in the coffee shop at 7:30; press conference at 10:00.","Fear and Loathing: On the Campaign Trail ’72","Hunter S. Thompson"},
["06:50"]={"Will, my fiancé, was coming from Boston on the \003six-fifty\004 train — the dawn train, the only train that still stopped in the small Ohio city where I lived.","Pretty Ice","Mary Robison"},
["06:51"]={"Moon Hartnell opened her eyes and reached for her phone. The screen said \0036:51 a.m.\004 on 14 February, Valentine’s Day. Most mornings, she would stay in bed until her alarm went off. Usually for a while after that, too — as long as it took Mum to bang on her door.","Kill Your Brother","Jack Heath"},
["06:52"]={"Sasha and Charlie caught the \0036:52\004 from Victoria to Merrifield the following morning, and arrived at the local Labour Party headquarters just before 8 a.m.","Heads You Win","Jeffrey Archer"},
["06:53"]={"So that was the key to asking my questions, to wait exactly 77 minutes before \003seven minutes to seven\004 and I would then get my answer.","The Quarter Moon","Stephanie Hudson"},
["06:54"]={"And to see if maybe — just maybe — she might have answered him, even though it was now \003six minutes before seven in the morning\004.","Her Billionaires","Julia Kent"},
["06:55"]={"At \0036:55 am\004 Lisa parked and took the lift from the frozen underground car park up to level 1 of Green Oaks Shopping Centre.","What Was Lost","Catherine O’Flynn"},
["06:57"]={"That meant that Helen must run and get the table set as quickly as possible as it was \003three minutes to seven\004.","The Carter Girls’ Mysterious Neighbors","Neil Speed"},
["06:58"]={"They waited. At exactly \003two minutes to seven\004, a white car came into view and pulled into the employee’s parking lot behind the building.","Small Sacrifices","Ann Rule"},
["06:59"]={"It was \0036:59 a.m.\004 on Maundy Thursday as Blomkvist and Berger let themselves into the “Millennium” offices.","The Girl Who Played with Fire","Stieg Larsson"},
